      "omegaBannerUrl": "",
      "readmeExcerpt": "# NoBodyPull\n\n## Purpose\n\nNoBodyPull is a plugin for XIVLauncher/Dalamud that helps prevent accidental pre-pulls by stopping movement into enemy aggro range before combat begins.\n\n## Features\n\n- Pre-pull aggro safety checks based on configured encounter ranges.\n- Movement inhibition when entering aggro range before combat starts.\n- Automatic disable once combat begins.\n- Lightweight behavior focused on preventing accidental pulls.\n\n## IMPORTANT\n\n- Movement inhibition is currently supported for keyboard movement.\n- Movement restriction can currently be bypassed by movement abilities (for example dashes and gap closers).\n- Movement restriction can also be bypassed by holding both mouse buttons for movement.\n- Controller movement is not currently supported by the movement inhibitor.\n\n## Usage\n\nThis plugin is designed to work with minimal setup.\n\n- During pre-pull, it checks your distance against known aggro thresholds.\n- If you move into danger range too early, it prevents that movement.\n- Once combat starts, intervention is disabled automatically.\n\nYou can configure behavior from the NoBodyPull settings window.\n\n## Installation\n\n### In-game (recommended)\n\n1. Open Dalamud settings with `/xlsettings`.\n2. Go to **Experimental** -> **Custom Plugin Repositories**.\n3. Add `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CaraMacchiato/DalamudRepo/main/repo.json`.\n4. Open Plugin Installer and install **NoBodyPull**.\n\n### Development build\n\n1. Open the solution in Visual Studio.\n2. Build `NoBodyPull.csproj`.\n3. Use local dev-plugin loading in Dalamud.\n\n## License\n\nCode and executable are covered under the MIT License.\n\nFinal Fantasy XIV (and any associated data used by this plugin) is owned by and copyright Square Enix.",
      "title": "NoBodyPull",
      "url": "https://github.com/CaraMacchiato/NoBodyPull"
    }
  },
